# 13. AdSense and Monetization Readiness

The project already includes:

- Legal pages
- SEO files
- AdSense-ready placeholders
- Responsive design
- Content pages

These are positive preparations, but AdSense approval should not be assumed.

Google’s current guidance emphasizes original, useful content, policy compliance, site ownership, a live and navigable website, and complete account setup. ([support.google.com](https://support.google.com/adsense/answer/9724?hl=en&utm_source=openai))

## 13.1 Original and useful content

The website should provide real value beyond a small collection of sample questions.

Improve:

- Number of questions
- Explanation quality
- Exam preparation guides
- Subject notes
- Study plans
- Practice resources
- Nepali educational content
- Helpful FAQs
- Original articles

Avoid thin pages that contain very little unique content.

## 13.2 Privacy policy

The privacy policy should clearly explain:

- What user data is collected
- Why it is collected
- How login data is used
- How test history is stored
- How cookies and local storage are used
- Whether analytics are used
- Whether advertising services are used
- How users can request data deletion
- How users can contact the operator

Google requires publishers to disclose relevant data collection and use associated with Google products and services. ([support.google.com](https://support.google.com/adsense/answer/10502938?hl=en&utm_source=openai))

## 13.3 Ads must not interfere with the app

Ads should not:

- Cover exam questions
- Cover answer buttons
- Interfere with navigation
- Cause accidental clicks
- Appear too close to important buttons
- Block the timer
- Appear over private user communication
- Refresh automatically without user action
- Open unexpectedly
- Encourage users to click ads

Google’s placement guidance specifically restricts ads that interfere with content or user interaction, including auto-refreshing and intrusive placements. ([support.google.com](https://support.google.com/adsense/answer/1346295?hl=en&utm_source=openai))

## 13.4 Do not place ads inside the active exam experience

The best user and policy approach is:

- Avoid ads while a timed test is active
- Avoid ads beside answer choices
- Avoid ads near the submit button
- Avoid ads on the result calculation screen
- Use ads mainly on home, article, subject, and informational pages
- Consider a clean exam interface for better user trust

## 13.5 ads.txt

The project has `robots.txt` and `sitemap.xml`, but an `ads.txt` file should be added when the AdSense account and publisher ID are available.

The file must contain the correct authorized seller information. Google recommends making the file reachable from the root domain and ensuring it returns a successful response. ([support.google.com](https://support.google.com/adsense/answer/9785052?hl=en&utm_source=openai))

Example format:

```text
google.com, pub-XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX, DIRECT, f08c47fec0942fa0
```

The actual publisher ID must be used. Do not copy the example value.

## 13.6 Site ownership and review

The production website should:

- Use a real custom domain
- Be publicly accessible
- Load correctly without broken pages
- Have working navigation
- Have complete legal pages
- Have original content
- Have no unfinished placeholder pages
- Have no broken links
- Have accurate contact information
- Be added and verified in AdSense

Google reviews a site before ads can be served and requires the site to be in an eligible status. ([support.google.com](https://support.google.com/adsense/answer/12131223?ctx=as2&utm_source=openai))

## 13.7 WebView and advertisements

The Android application should not simply copy web advertisements into the WebView without reviewing the applicable Google policies and approved implementation approach.

The website and Android application should have separate monetization planning:

- Website: AdSense-compatible web implementation
- Android app: Appropriate mobile-app advertising solution and policy review

Google notes that content displayed inside WebView remains subject to applicable content requirements, and ad implementation must use approved technologies and placements. ([support.google.com](https://support.google.com/adsense/answer/1346295?hl=en&utm_source=openai))

